# .forge/conformance-surfaces — the forge-skill's conformance-surface declaration.
#
# Distinct from .forge/critical-surfaces (which names silent-failure surfaces for
# the commit-hook gauge): this manifest names the surfaces a CONFORMANCE slice
# exercises, so --ledger-check --stage design/--range grades the per-slice class
# matrix (.forge/conformance/<slice>) against the touched owner-surfaces.
#
# The obligation is forge-skill process authority (the T2 conformance loop, per
# the user-level AGENTS.md), NOT a landed repo document — the product-contract
# authority for the harness itself is ADR-0013 (corpus-as-acceptance-oracle),
# which superseded the pre-ADR "ROADMAP RA2 + charter §6 invariant 2" pointer.
#
# This manifest is FORCE-TRACKED (git add -f) past the broad .forge/ ignore.
# Globs match the full repo-relative path; `*` matches any chars including `/`;
# a bare-dir prefix also matches.

# RA2 — the conformance round-trip harness. The one surface it exercises is
# BAP's envelope verifier (check_envelope/2) + the grant-only verifier
# (verify_grant/3 for the grant_time_cases). The harness file IS the surface.
test/bounded_authority_report_adapter/conformance_roundtrip_test.exs

